Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:39:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 081/154] feat(hotkeys): Cmd+D pins the shown tab, and Cmd+1..9
 open the favourites
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cmd+D: the core shipped pinToggleTab on cmd+d since the hotkey store was
written, so the Inputs pane listed it while no native row ran it and the
key reached Bookmark This Tab. A regular row pins through
atrium_core_pin_tab_by_tab_id, a pinned row unpins through
atrium_core_unpin_tab, the two entry points the drag-drop path uses.

Cmd+1..9: no action claimed the digits, so they reached IDC_SELECT_TAB_N
and picked a tab of the shared strip, whose order is open order across
every space. The core now binds goToSidebarItem1..8 and
goToSidebarItemLast to the chords and drops the goToSpaceN rows that
nothing ever ran. The action re-enters the favourite tile's own click
message, so live, cross-space and cold tiles behave as a click.

One commit for both: they share the enum, the table and the route file
at line level.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
